# External dead-man's-switch for health-watch.sh. Copy to
# /etc/healthchecks-ping.env, fill in your own check's URL, chmod 600.
#
# Get one free at https://healthchecks.io — create a Check, copy its ping
# URL. Set the check's Period to match health-watch.timer (currently
# hourly) and its Grace period to something like 20-30 minutes, so a single
# slow run doesn't trigger a false alarm.
#
# health-watch.sh pings this URL once per unattended run, unconditionally,
# regardless of what it found. If the file is missing, health-watch.sh
# silently skips this step — nothing breaks on a host that hasn't set it up.
HEALTHCHECKS_PING_URL=
